  "identity": {
    "playing_style": "Gasperini imported his Atalanta model: a 3-4-2-1 that presses man-for-man across the whole pitch, defends on a very advanced line and attacks with extreme dynamism and verticality, with wide centre-backs and wing-backs (Wesley, Molina, Rensch) licensed to arrive in the box. 2025/26 delivered 3rd place (70 pts, 53-35) — a return to the Champions League — but early exits in the Coppa Italia (Torino) and Europa League (Bologna). The 2026 window added a No. 9 who fits the press (Castro), two centre-backs comfortable 1v1 (Koulierakis, Balerdi), a right wing-back (Molina) and Gasperini's old lieutenant De Roon, and Malen's January loan was converted for EUR 25m.",
    "principles": [
      "Gasperini system built for man-marking pressers and athletic wide defenders",
      "American private ownership (Friedkin) funding a EUR 1bn private stadium and a rebuild under UEFA settlement limits",
      "Argentine core (Dybala, Soulé, Castro, Balerdi, Molina) around Italian veterans (Pellegrini, Cristante, Mancini)",
      "sell or loan misfits quickly (Dovbyk, Vaz, Baldanzi, Ziolkowski, Angeliño)",
      "youth from Trigoria given senior slots (Pisilli, Lulli, Arena, De Marzi)"
    ],
    "club_character": "Owned 95.97% by The Friedkin Group (Dan Friedkin president) since 2020; one of Italy's most passionate and demanding fanbases, with heavy Roman media pressure and a Curva Sud that has repeatedly clashed with ownership over communication. The privately funded 60,605-seat Pietralata stadium (EUR 1.047bn) received Capitoline Assembly feasibility approval in March 2026 with groundbreaking targeted for 2027.",
    "ownership": "private (The Friedkin Group, 95.97%)",
    "political_and_social_context": "Publicly documented: Roma operate under a UEFA financial settlement agreement and were fined EUR 3m for missing interim targets; the Pietralata stadium project has been the subject of years of municipal politics and local opposition; the club runs long-standing anti-racism and community programmes and has periodically been sanctioned for discriminatory chanting by sections of fans. No further institution-level positions verified this session.",
    "languages": [
      "it",
      "en",
      "es"
    ],
    "wage_structure": "hierarchical but compressed by the UEFA settlement: Dybala renewed to 2027 on reduced terms; new signings on ~EUR 2-2.5m net (Castro 2m, Molina 2.5m, De Roon 2m)",
    "transfer_policy": "Buy prime-age or young Serie A / Bundesliga / Ligue 1 starters with resale value (Castro 22, Koulierakis, Vaz 19), use loans with conditional obligations (Malen, Balerdi, Ferguson) to spread cost under settlement limits, and offload non-fits (Dovbyk loan, Vaz loan to Hull with EUR 30m option).",
    "injury_management_reputation": null
